      "page_title": "Everyday Recipes & Decision Table",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Interruption"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash push -u -m \"wip: checkout flow\"",
            "# fix the bug, commit it",
            "git stash pop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Test Only The Staged Half"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git add -p",
            "git stash push --keep-index -m \"rest\"",
            "npm test && git commit",
            "git stash pop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Wrong Branch, Right Fix"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash -u",
            "git switch -c correct-branch",
            "git stash pop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rescue And Recover"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash branch salvage stash@{0}",
            "# merge or cherry-pick from salvage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worktree Recipes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git fetch origin pull/123/head:pr-123",
            "git worktree add ../review pr-123",
            "git worktree remove ../review"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Side by side: add `../v1 v1.0` and `../v2 v2.0`",
            "Run both, diff the outputs directly",
            "Bisect: `git worktree add ../bisect --detach`",
            "Bisect refs are per-worktree — workspace safe",
            "Sweep: `list`, `remove` each, `prune`, then `stash list`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Two Models",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stash: hidden 2-or-3-parent commits in `refs/stash`",
            "Indexed by reflog position, one working tree",
            "Worktree: extra directory, own HEAD and index",
            "Shared object store, listed in `.git/worktrees/`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "apply vs pop, Final Word"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`apply` keeps the entry, always",
            "`pop` drops it on a clean apply only",
            "After any conflict, verify `git stash list` yourself"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Decision Table"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Choose"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<10 min, small diff",
              "stash"
            ],
            [
              "Parallel or hot build",
              "worktree"
            ],
            [
              "Side-by-side compare",
              "worktree"
            ],
            [
              "Isolated config/hooks",
              "separate clone"
            ],
            [
              "Clean tree, moving",
              "git switch"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stash Flags At A Glance"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Adds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "-u",
              "untracked files"
            ],
            [
              "-a",
              "untracked + ignored"
            ],
            [
              "-k",
              "keeps staged live"
            ],
            [
              "--staged",
              "staged only"
            ],
            [
              "-p",
              "chosen hunks"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Worked Examples & Worktree Verbs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: Hot Build"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# 10-min build, feature tree stays hot",
            "git worktree add -b fix-88 ../fix main",
            "cd ../fix && npm ci && npm test",
            "git push -u origin fix-88",
            "git worktree remove ../fix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Your feature tree keeps its warm caches",
            "No `node_modules` reinstall on the main tree",
            "Two builds run at once over one object store",
            "Nothing was stashed, so nothing can be lost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Interrupt Without Losing Files"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash push -u -m \"wip: cart\"",
            "git switch main && git pull --rebase",
            "git switch -      # back to feature",
            "git stash pop     # then check the list"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Mind the index",
          "text": "Staged work returns unstaged unless you pass `--index`, and `--index` fails outright when the index state cannot be rebuilt."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worktree Verbs"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Verb",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "add",
              "new checkout"
            ],
            [
              "list",
              "path, HEAD, branch"
            ],
            [
              "remove",
              "clean delete"
            ],
            [
              "prune",
              "clears stale entries"
            ],
            [
              "lock",
              "blocks prune"
            ],
            [
              "move",
              "relocates a worktree"
            ],
            [
              "repair",
              "fixes path pointers"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading Worktree List"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git worktree list",
            "/repo  9f2c1 [main]",
            "/hf    3a71b [hotfix-501]",
            "/rev   4c0de (detached HEAD)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`(detached HEAD)` marks a throwaway checkout",
            "A row whose directory is gone stays until `prune`",
            "`--porcelain` gives a __stable__ parseable form"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Interrupt, Hotfix, Resume"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git worktree add -b hotfix-501 ../hf main",
            "# fix, test, push from ../hf",
            "git worktree remove ../hf",
            "# the feature tree was never touched"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Habits That Prevent Pain"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Always label with `-m`",
            "Always include untracked with `-u`",
            "The defaults are the source of most stash pain"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Safe Scripting & Final Recall",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git config --global alias.sp \\",
            "  'stash push -u -m'",
            "git sp \"wip: checkout flow\""
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Dropped entries survive until gc prunes them (~2 weeks)",
            "`git fsck --unreachable` still finds them",
            "`git stash create` prints a SHA, touches nothing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Never-Break Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Never treat `refs/stash` as storage",
            "Promote value to a branch: `git stash branch`",
            "Always remove with `git worktree remove`",
            "`prune` after any manual directory deletion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stash Anatomy Recall",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Part",
            "Holds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "tree",
              "working tree"
            ],
            [
              "parent 1",
              "HEAD at push"
            ],
            [
              "parent 2",
              "index state"
            ],
            [
              "parent 3",
              "untracked (-u)"
            ],
            [
              "stack",
              "refs/stash reflog"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scripting Around The Stack",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "tag=\"wip-$$\"   # unique label",
            "git stash push -u -m \"$tag\"",
            "sha=$(git stash list --format='%H %gs' |",
            "  grep -F \"$tag\" | cut -d' ' -f1)",
            "git stash apply \"$sha\"  # not pop"
          ],
          "note": "one shared stack per repo"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==One `refs/stash`== is shared by every worktree",
            "So a bare `pop` can grab **someone else's** entry",
            "Apply by SHA, never by `stash@{n}` — indices shift"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Five commands to keep",
          "items": [
            "`git stash push -u -m msg`",
            "`git stash apply` then `drop`",
            "`git stash branch <name>`",
            "`git worktree add -b br ../dir`",
            "`git worktree list / remove / prune`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Recall line",
          "text": "Stash time-multiplexes one tree; worktrees space-multiplex many trees over one history."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Your boss pings you mid-refactor and `git switch` refuses to move. Git has two answers, and they are not interchangeable: stash time-multiplexes one working tree, worktrees space-multiplex many checkouts over one object database. Part 2 of GIT FIELD NOTES covers the everyday recipes, a decision table, worked examples, the worktree verbs, and scripting safely around the one shared stash stack.",
